.TH SCX_LAYERED 8 "" "scx" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
scx_layered \- configurable layered sched_ext scheduler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scx_layered
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Layered classifies tasks into layers and applies configurable CPU allocation
and scheduling rules to each layer.
.PP
Loading this scheduler requires a kernel with CONFIG_SCHED_CLASS_EXT and
a process with privileges to load and attach BPF programs.
.PP
The package installs example layer configurations under
\fI/usr/share/doc/scx-layered/examples/\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display the options supported by this command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/kernel/sched_ext/state
Current sched_ext state.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/scx-layered/
Upstream scheduler documentation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://docs.kernel.org/scheduler/sched-ext.html
Linux kernel sched_ext documentation
.UE
